{"id": "JAH-SIG-TELEMETR-000001", "slug": "tool-telemetry-intelligence-analyzer-signature", "title": "Telemetry Intelligence Analyzer \u2014 Overview and definition", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "tool database record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature methods and framings developed for the JAH system, labeled Signature throughout. Processes spacecraft measurements to identify trends and anomalies. The Telemetry Intelligence Analyzer ingests streams of spacecraft measurements \u2014 temperatures, voltages, pressures \u2014 and finds trends, drift, and anomalies: rolling statistics, z-score outlier flags, and trend-slope estimates per channel. It distinguishes sensor noise from real drift and reports every flag with the data window that produced it. Engineering analysis of measurement data. Capability specification and design target: this database describes what the tool must do, not a claim of implementation or deployment. Defensive and engineering content only \u2014 no weapon-targeting or attack-execution content.", "capabilities": ["Rolling statistics per telemetry channel", "Z-score anomaly flagging", "Trend and drift slope estimation", "Noise-vs-drift discrimination", "Flag reports with data windows"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Tool overview and capability inventory", "code": "J({tool:TOOL.name,capabilities:TOOL.capabilities,count:TOOL.capabilities.length});assert(TOOL.capabilities.length>=5,'caps');", "verified_output": "{\"tool\":\"Telemetry Intelligence Analyzer\",\"capabilities\":[\"Rolling statistics per telemetry channel\",\"Z-score anomaly flagging\",\"Trend and drift slope estimation\",\"Noise-vs-drift discrimination\",\"Flag reports with data windows\"],\"count\":5}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "catalog-100-darpa-nasa-grade-tools-2026-10-21.txt", "last_v